(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The C API's natives queue 594 adds for _testcapi's rows (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 594\"), each written"] [4 1 "// after CPython 3.14.10's function of the same name: Py_FatalError and _Py_FatalErrorFunc (Python/pylifecycle.c's"] [5 1 "// fatal_error with _Py_DumpExtensionModules), and the thread state Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS gives up (PyEval_SaveThread,"] [6 1 "// PyEval_RestoreThread), whose absence a C API call that needs it reports as PyThreadState_Get's fatal error. The PSF's"] [7 1 "// license (LICENSE.md)."] [18 1 "// released are the C threads inside Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS (PyEval_SaveThread to PyEval_RestoreThread): no thread"] [19 1 "// state is current there."] [22 1 "// extensionModules is _Py_DumpExtensionModules' list: the names of sys.modules' modules made from a PyModuleDef (the C"] [23 1 "// world's, and the built-in modules), but the standard library's (sys.stdlib_module_names), in sys.modules' order."] [42 3 "// a module of a PyModuleDef: the world's (moduleDefs), or a built-in one (pyi's built-ins, the world's _testcapi"] [43 3 "// among them, are CPython's modules of a definition)"] [63 1 "// fatalError is fatal_error(fd, header, prefix, msg, status): the process ends by abort()."] [68 1 "// noTstate is _Py_EnsureTstateNotNULL's check of a call that needs the thread state, as PyThreadState_Get reports it"] [69 1 "// when C called the API inside Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS (test_capi's test_no_FatalError_infinite_loop)."] [79 2 "// Py_FatalError(msg) (the limited API's function) and _Py_FatalErrorFunc(func, msg) (the macro's: its caller's"] [80 2 "// __func__ as the prefix)"] [93 2 "// PyEval_SaveThread: the thread state given up (pyi's world keeps one), PyEval_RestoreThread: taken again"] [103 2 "// PyGILState_Ensure inside Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS takes the thread state again (PyGILState_UNLOCKED, 1), its"] [104 2 "// PyGILState_Release(UNLOCKED) gives it up again"] [120 2 "// PyThreadState_Get and _GetUnchecked: tstate->context written (tsContextWrite)"] [129 2 "// PyUnstable_Object_ClearWeakRefsNoCallbacks (Objects/weakrefobject.c): the referent's weak references cleared, no"] [130 2 "// callback called, nothing for a type without weak references"] [137 2 "// the error indicator's setters need the thread state (errors.c's _PyThreadState_GET, then the exception's"] [138 2 "// creation)"] [140 16 "// a wrapper above (PyThreadState_Get's context), else the native"] [155 1 "// The debug hooks on the allocators (Objects/obmalloc.c's _PyMem_DebugRaw*, PYTHONMALLOC=debug, malloc_debug,"] [156 1 "// pymalloc_debug or mimalloc_debug): a block of the RAW ('r') and MEM ('m') domains is laid out as CPython's,"] [157 1 "// [size (8, big-endian), the API id, 7 FORBIDDENBYTEs, the data (CLEANBYTEs), 8 FORBIDDENBYTEs], checked when freed"] [158 1 "// or reallocated (a wrong API or a pad byte overwritten: the block dumped, then the fatal error), and MEM and OBJ"] [159 1 "// ('o') check the thread state (_PyMem_DebugCheckGIL). OBJ's blocks keep the world's layout: pyi's C objects are"] [160 1 "// made and freed through it."] [170 21 "// 0 unknown, 1 on, 2 off"] [175 1 "// debugHooks is whether PYTHONMALLOC asks for the debug hooks."] [187 1 "// debugCheckGIL is _PyMem_DebugCheckGIL."] [194 1 "// debugAlloc is _PyMem_DebugRawAlloc over the world's allocator (raw: the domain's default allocation of size bytes)."] [227 1 "// debugSize is the size a debug block's header records."] [236 1 "// debugDump is _PyObject_DebugDumpAddress, then _PyMem_DumpTraceback's line without tracemalloc's traces."] [306 1 "// debugCheckAddress is _PyMem_DebugCheckAddress: the API id, the leading and the trailing pad bytes."] [327 1 "// debugDomain is the domain d's operation i (malloc, calloc, realloc, free) through the debug hooks over the world's"] [328 1 "// allocator; ok false when the hooks are off or the block is none of theirs (the domain's default runs)."] [379 1 "// debugFree fills a checked block with DEADBYTEs and gives it back to the world's allocator."] [387 1 "// Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_VECTORCALL across the classes over C types (Objects/typeobject.c, queue 594: test_call's TestPEP590):"] [388 1 "// a class inherits it from its C base when no class before that base in its MRO defines __call__ (inherit_slots), and"] [389 1 "// setting __call__ on a C type clears it there (update_one_slot's slot_tp_call: a generic __call__ is incompatible"] [390 1 "// with vectorcall), the type then called through its __call__, its subclasses' slots refilled."] [406 1 "// callSetOnCType is ExtTypeAttrSet: __call__ set on a C type."] [421 2 "// the classes over t that C has seen: their tp_flags again (a C type of their own keeps its own)"] [447 2 "// a C-born object keeps its Go finalizer on its life (newCObj), not on itself: py tracks it for its weak references"] [451 1 "// tstate->context (Include/cpython/pystate.h, LP64: offsetof(PyThreadState, context), gcc on CPython 3.14.10's headers):"] [452 1 "// the thread's current context, written when C fetches the thread state and held while it is there; a context C"] [453 1 "// cleared (Py_CLEAR(tstate->context): _testcapi's clear_context_stack, queue 594) is the thread's no more. A context's"] [454 1 "// ctx_prev (offset 16) is its proxy's zeroed word."] [459 1 "// tsContextWrite writes the thread's context into the thread state at ts."] [479 1 "// tsContextDone takes the thread state's context back when the outermost C entry returns (capiLeave): cleared by C,"] [480 1 "// the thread's is cleared."] [491 27 "// C's Py_CLEAR gave the reference back"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 39] [53 35] [132 23] [205 12] [205 26] [209 23] [209 39] [216 20] [216 32] [219 20] [219 34] [254 24] [254 32] [288 7] [288 31] [296 8] [296 23] [309 32] [396 21] [417 25] [423 26] [432 34] [448 60] [465 28]]} (go/file "capi_fatal.go" :imports [

